<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shwebo</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Moksobo</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shwebo is a town in the Sagaing Region of upper Myanmar, north-west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mandalay">Mandalay</a>. Formerly the village of Moksobo, it was the home of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alaungpaya">Alaungpaya</a>, who rose there in 1752 against the Restored Hanthawaddy Kingdom, founded the Konbaung dynasty and made it his first capital. The ancient Pyu city of Halin lies nearby.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/shwebo.jpg" alt="Shwebo" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ninjastrikers · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Shwebo_Palace.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
